and there wouldn't be enough X to go around.

267
00:10:01,120 --> 00:10:03,480
And if the price of Y were really low,

268
00:10:03,480 --> 00:10:05,360
then everyone would wanna go and buy a lot of Y,

269
00:10:05,360 --> 00:10:07,480
and there wouldn't be enough Y to go around.

270
00:10:07,480 --> 00:10:10,080
So the only equilibrium that makes the world stable

271
00:10:10,080 --> 00:10:14,160
is one where the amount of X that people start with

272
00:10:14,160 --> 00:10:16,360
is the amount that they want to end up with.

273
00:10:17,280 --> 00:10:18,360
All right, so is that obvious?

274
00:10:18,360 --> 00:10:20,920
It's not obvious because how much X you want

275
00:10:20,920 --> 00:10:22,520
depends on what prices.

276
00:10:22,520 --> 00:10:23,960
A low price of X, you want a lot of X.

277
00:10:23,960 --> 00:10:26,920
A high price of X, you wanna have less X.

278
00:10:26,920 --> 00:10:28,480
So if there's a low price of X, you wanna buy it,

279
00:10:28,480 --> 00:10:30,840
a high price of X, you wanna sell it.

280
00:10:30,840 --> 00:10:32,080
All right, and what is it gonna take

281
00:10:32,080 --> 00:10:33,560
to make this world stable?

282
00:10:33,560 --> 00:10:35,160
We're gonna need to have the price of X

283
00:10:35,160 --> 00:10:37,640
and the price of Y just right, just right

284
00:10:37,640 --> 00:10:40,560
so that people are content with where they started.

285
00:10:40,560 --> 00:10:42,040
And why do they have to be content with where they started?

286
00:10:42,040 --> 00:10:43,120
Because we assumed everyone starts

287
00:10:43,120 --> 00:10:45,640
with identical preferences and endowments.

288
00:10:45,640 --> 00:10:47,640
So this is gonna be a world where nobody wants,

