00:10:53,160 --> 00:10:55,880
We've decided it to be weird to prove a point,

293
00:10:55,880 --> 00:10:59,040
and then we will complicate it to make it more reasonable.

294
00:10:59,880 --> 00:11:02,440
All right, all right, so anyway,

295
00:11:02,440 --> 00:11:04,240
so the situation is saying it will only, at price,

296
00:11:04,240 --> 00:11:06,840
induce everyone to consume their initial endowments.

297
00:11:06,840 --> 00:11:08,680
So a formula we can do is this.

298
00:11:08,680 --> 00:11:10,880
So we can substitute out for Y by noting

299
00:11:10,880 --> 00:11:14,120
that Y is gonna be equal to your total income

300
00:11:14,960 --> 00:11:18,080
minus the price of X times the quantity of X that you buy,

301
00:11:18,080 --> 00:11:19,800
all of it over the price of Y.

302
00:11:19,800 --> 00:11:21,360
And this is just from the budget constraints.

303
00:11:21,360 --> 00:11:23,720
So you see, we can go and multiply both sides by PY,

304
00:11:23,720 --> 00:11:28,480
and we have PY times X is equal to income minus PX times X.

305
00:11:28,480 --> 00:11:30,240
We can then put that over, we can say your income

