00:11:43,360 --> 00:11:46,120
your income is just going to be equal to

311
00:11:47,640 --> 00:11:49,240
price of X times X bar.

312
00:11:49,240 --> 00:11:51,000
So whenever we put a bar over something,

313
00:11:51,000 --> 00:11:52,760
it indicates an initial endowment.

314
00:11:52,760 --> 00:11:54,600
Yes, the amount that you start with.

315
00:11:54,600 --> 00:11:59,600
So we have PX times X bar plus BY times Y bar.

316
00:11:59,600 --> 00:12:02,880
Oh yeah, so this here is,

317
00:12:02,880 --> 00:12:04,440
it needs to have an equilibrium,

318
00:12:04,440 --> 00:12:07,040
and this is just what your income's going to be.

319
00:12:07,040 --> 00:12:11,000
All right, okay, so we can go and plug all of this in

320
00:12:11,000 --> 00:12:14,520
to here, right, and then we're gonna see

321
00:12:14,520 --> 00:12:17,640
the agents are gonna maximize A times the log of X

322
00:12:17,640 --> 00:12:19,800
plus B times the log of,

323
00:12:19,800 --> 00:12:21,400
and then we substitute out for everything.

324
00:12:21,400 --> 00:12:24,960
So we can substitute income into there,

325
00:12:24,960 --> 00:12:26,800
and then put Y into there,

326
00:12:26,800 --> 00:12:29,240
and then we get this equation here.

327
00:12:29,240 --> 00:12:33,120
All right, and then we differentiate, right,

328
00:12:33,120 --> 00:12:34,080
and when you differentiate,

329
00:12:34,080 --> 00:12:36,200
we learn that the amount of X that you want

330
00:12:36,200 --> 00:12:41,200
is gonna be equal to A over B times PY over PX times Y,

331
00:12:42,120 --> 00:12:45,120
and then, since there's only two things

332
00:12:45,120 --> 00:12:45,960
to do with your income,

333
00:12:45,960 --> 00:12:48,040
there's never any reason not to spend this, right?

334
00:12:48,040 --> 00:12:49,920
It's a very simple world, there's only two things to do.

335
00:12:49,920 --> 00:12:50,760
So you might.

336
00:12:50,760 --> 00:12:52,720
So it's not partial with respect to X, so.

337
00:12:52,720 --> 00:12:55,120
Yes, yes, yes, yes, that's right.

338
00:12:55,120 --> 00:12:58,600
All right, so agents are gonna consume all their income,

339
00:12:58,600 --> 00:13:01,920
so you might remember working with this utility function

